 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity**: $O(1)$ per voxel, involving a few trigonometric evaluations and arithmetic operations.
-- **Memory Complexity**: $O(1)$, storing only four constant vectors.
-- **Strengths**: Extremely compact definition; produces smooth, visually pleasing gradients with minimal parameters; easy to implement in shaders [S1, unofficial].
-- **Limitations**: Limited control over specific color transitions compared to multi-component basis functions; may not highlight specific data ranges as effectively as Gaussian methods [S1, unofficial].
-- **When to use**: General-purpose volume rendering where aesthetic appeal and simplicity are prioritized over precise data-driven color mapping.
+**Time and Memory Complexity:**
+- Time: $O(1)$ per sample. Requires three cosine evaluations and basic arithmetic.
+- Memory: $O(1)$ for parameter storage.
+
+**Strengths and Limitations:**
+- Strengths: Produces smooth, aesthetically pleasing gradients with minimal computational cost. The phase offsets create complex color variations from simple parameters.
+- Limitations: The output is perceptually non-uniform in some regions due to the nature of cosine interference. It does not inherently support multi-modal data separation like Gaussian functions.
+
+**When to Use:**
+- Suitable for general volume visualization where smooth color transitions are desired and computational efficiency is critical.
+- Not suitable when precise perceptual uniformity or distinct multi-modal separation is required.
 
 ## Background
-The method was popularized by Inigo Quilez in the context of procedural shading and raymarching, where it is used to generate aesthetically pleasing color palettes from simple scalar inputs [S1, unofficial]. It has been adapted for volume rendering as a parametric transfer function generation technique.
+The method was popularized by Inigo Quilez in the context of GLSL shader programming for procedural color generation [S1, unofficial]. It is widely used in real-time graphics and volume rendering shaders due to its simplicity and visual quality.
 
